Each moving particle is a group of refugees or asylum-seekers travelling from their country of origin to their country of asylum, as recorded by the UNHCR for the selected year. The brighter and thicker a corridor, the more people it carries, and the colour tells the continent of origin. Move the year slider to watch crises appear and fade, and hover a country to read how many people left it or found refuge there. Only corridors above 5,000 people are drawn.


